 "paragraphs": [
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p001.s01",
     "source": "If the possibility of Ghost Laying was believed in, so also was the possibility of raising Evil Spirits."
    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s02",
     "source": "This faith dates from olden times."
    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s03",
     "source": "Shakespeare, to this, as to most other popular notions, has given a place in his immortal plays."
    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s04",
     "source": "Speaking rightly in the name of “Glendower,” a Welshman, conversant with Ghosts and Goblins, the poet makes him say:—"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p001"
