    }
   ],
   "id": "p281"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p282.s01",
     "source": "This idea has continued right to our own days, and adepts in the black art have affirmed that they possess this power."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p282"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p283.s01",
     "source": "Doctor Bennion, a gentleman well known in his lifetime in and about Oswestry, was thought to be able to raise Devils."
    },
    {
     "id": "p283.s02",
     "source": "I find in the history of Ffynnon Elian , p. 12, that the doctor visited John Evans, the last custodian of the well, and taught him how to accomplish this feat."
    },
    {
     "id": "p283.s03",
     "source": "For the benefit of those anxious to obtain this power, I will give the doctor’s recipe:—“Publish it abroad that you can raise the Devil, and the country will believe you, and will credit you with many miracles."
    },
    {
     "id": "p283.s04",
     "source": "All that you have to do afterwards is to be silent, and you will then be as good a raiser of Devils as I am, and I as good as you.”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p283"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p284.s01",
     "source": "Evans confesses that he acted according to the astute doctor’s advice, and he adds—“The people in a very short time spoke much about me, and they soon came to intrust everything to me, their conduct frightened me, for they looked upon me as if I were a god.”"
    },
    {
     "id": "p284.s02",
     "source": "This man died August 14th, 1858."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p284"
  }
 ]
}